<title>BELGIUM: EU says Danish shipyard must repay state aid.</title>
<headline>EU says Danish shipyard must repay state aid.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday that Danish group A.P.Moeller's Odense Shipyard must repay around one million crowns ($159,000) in excessive state subsidies granted over five contracts in 1992.</p>
<p>The commission said in a statement that its decision was the result of a larger investigation into the financing of shipbuilding in Denmark during 1987-1993.</p>
<p>&quot;The Commission has examined 58 contracts and found that 53 of them respected the aid ceiling in force at the time that the contract was signed, while in five cases the aid granted exceeded that ceiling,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>--Fredrik Dahl, Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 6811 ($ = 6.284 Danish Crowns)</p>
</text>
